        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.523,
            0.027,
            0.845,
            0.045
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter 3 — Health: The Ultimate Treasure"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.082,
            0.743,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. Diseases can be broadly grouped into communicable and non-communicable diseases. From the options given below, identify the non-communicable diseases. (i) Typhoid (ii) Asthma (iii) Diabetes (iv) Measles (a) (i) and (ii) (b) (ii) and (iii) (c) (i) and (iv) (d) (ii) and (iv)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.196,
            0.744,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. There is a flu outbreak in your school. Several classmates are absent, while some are still coming to school coughing and sneezing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.262,
            0.743,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What immediate actions should the school take to prevent further spread?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.307,
            0.743,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If your classmate, who shares the bench with you, starts showing symptoms of the flu, how can you respond in a considerate way without being rude or hurtful?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.373,
            0.743,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) How can you protect yourself and others from getting infected in this situation?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.418,
            0.743,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Your family is planning to travel to another city where malaria is prevalent."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.463,
            0.742,
            0.506
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What precautions should you take before, during, and after the trip?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.508,
            0.743,
            0.551
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) How can you explain the importance of mosquito nets or repellents to your sibling?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.553,
            0.743,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) What could happen if travellers ignore health advisories in such areas?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.598,
            0.743,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Your uncle has started smoking just to fit in with his friends, even though it is well known that smoking can seriously harm health and even cause death."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.664,
            0.743,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What would you say to him to make him stop, without being rude?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.709,
            0.743,
            0.751
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What would you do if your friend offers you a cigarette at a party?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.754,
            0.743,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) How can schools help prevent students from indulging in such harmful habits?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.799,
            0.745,
            0.885
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Saniya claims to her friend Vinita that “Antibiotics can cure any infection, so we don’t need to worry about diseases.” What question(s) can Vinita ask her to help Saniya understand that her statement is incorrect?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
